            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Three things, none of them visible at the time: fine grit erodes the impeller blades, dust packs into the motor bearings and windings where it raises operating temperature and shortens motor life, and the finest particles are exhausted back into the room at head height. Mineral dust does all three quickly."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a filter to vacuum water with a shop vac?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No \u2014 you must remove the pleated cartridge for wet pickup. Fit the foam sleeve if your model uses one; it is a splash barrier that keeps droplets out of the motor housing rather than a filter. Water pickup creates no airborne dust, so there is nothing for a filter to capture."
