          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Filter out for water, filter in for everything dry</strong> — and add a collection bag whenever the dust is fine. That combination protects the motor, keeps airflow high through a whole job, and keeps the particles that matter out of the air you are standing in.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If the reason you are running bare is a filter that keeps clogging, the answer is a bag and a spare cartridge on the shelf. <strong class="text-white">Both cost less than one motor.</strong>
